- "Descend into a dict or list only when both sides at that path are the same kind of container." So if both are dicts → compare per key. If both are lists → compare per index. Otherwise, if equal → no output; if different → `~ PATH: OLD -> NEW`.

Wait — what about the case where both are dicts but equal? In that case there are no differences internally anyway, so descending produces nothing. So no problem. But "descend only when both are the same kind of container" — if both are the same kind of container, descend; otherwise compare equality; if not equal, output `~`.

- Sorting: sorted list of strings. Sort the final strings lexicographically. Check test_dict_add_remove_change: ["+ $.c: 4", "- $.a: 1", "~ $.b: 2 -> 3"] — '+' (0x2B) < '-' (0x2D) < '~' (0x7E). Yes, simple sorted() works.

